{"description": "The Hobbit is a tale of high adventure, undertaken by a company of dwarves in search of dragon-guarded gold. A reluctant partner in this perilous quest is Bilbo Baggins, a comfort-loving unambitious hobbit, who surprises even himself by his resourcefulness and skill as a burglar.

Encounters with trolls, goblins, dwarves, elves, and giant spiders, conversations with the dragon, Smaug, and a rather unwilling presence at the Battle of Five Armies are just some of the adventures that befall Bilbo.

Bilbo Baggins has taken his place among the ranks of the immortals of children’s fiction. Written by Professor Tolkien for his children, The Hobbit met with instant critical acclaim when published.", "authors": [{"author": {"key": "/authors/OL26320A"}, "type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}}], "key": "/works/OL27482W", "title": "The Hobbit", "type": {"key": "/type/work"}, "links": [{"title": "Tolkien Estate | The Hobbit", "url": "http://www.tolkienestate.com/en/writing/tales-of-middle-earth/the-hobbit.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "The Hobbit by JRR Tolkien - review", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/childrens-books-site/2013/jul/18/review-the-hobbit-jrr-tolkien", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "The Hobbit by JRR Tolkien book review", "url": "http://www.fantasybookreview.co.uk/JRR-Tolkien/The-Hobbit.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "The Hobbit at 80: What were JRR Tolkien's inspirations behind his first fantasy tale of Middle Earth?", "url": "https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/books/news/the-hobbit-80-jrr-tolkien-anniversary-published-lord-of-the-rings-middle-earth-fantasy-inspiration-a7957321.html", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}, {"title": "The Hobbit by J.R.R. Tolkien - Tolkien Library", "url": "http://www.tolkienlibrary.com/booksbytolkien/hobbit/description.htm", "type": {"key": "/type/link"}}], "covers": [14627509], "first_sentence": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "In a hole in the ground there lived a hobbit. Not a nasty diry wet hole, filled with ends of worms and an oozy smell..."}, "subject_places": ["Middle-earth", "Lonely Mountain", "Lake-town", "Rivendell", "Iron Hills", "Misty Mountains", "Mirkwood", "the Shire"], "first_publish_date": "January 1938", "subject_people": ["Bilbo Baggins", "Gandalf", "Thorin Oakenshield", "Fili", "Kili", "Balin", "Dwalin", "Oin", "Gloin", "Dori", "Nori", "Ori", "Bifur", "Bofur", "Bombur", "Lake-men", "Smaug", "Wargs", "Wood-elves", "Beorn", "Bard the Bowman", "E